{#- What a codec's owned form asks of a storage profile (docs/adr/0077 §7): a tag
    type for each variable field, what `Inline` holds it in, and one trait a site
    names for all of it. A supertrait is implied where the trait is named, and a
    struct's `where` clause is not. A deployment answers for the tags from a file
    of its own, so no capacity of one enters this tree.

    A child codec compiled under a build feature cannot be a plain supertrait,
    since an attribute does not go on one: it is reached through a trait of its
    own, which asks for nothing in a build without the feature (docs/adr/0072). #}
{#- How the inline profile `profile` holds the field `field`, named by the path
    `tag`: in a container of `field.capacity`. `Inline` in the tree and a
    deployment in its own file both answer through this one form. #}
{%- macro holds(runtime, profile, tag, field) %}
impl {{ runtime }}::Holds{{ field.kind }}<{{ tag }}> for {{ profile }} {
{% if field.kind == "List" %}
    type List<T> = ::sce_forge_runtime::heapless::Vec<T, {{ field.capacity }}> where T: Default + ::core::fmt::Debug + Clone + PartialEq;
{% elif field.kind == "Str" %}
    type Str = {{ runtime }}::InlineStr<{{ field.capacity }}>;
{% else %}
    type Bytes = {{ runtime }}::InlineBytes<{{ field.capacity }}>;
{% endif %}
}
{%- endmacro %}
{#- How the heap node `profile` holds the field `field` (docs/adr/0077 §7): on
    the heap, to `field.capacity`, what the field holds (the deployment's policy
    limit, or the field's bound where it gives none), and refused past it as an
    inline node refuses past its array; growing where the protocol states no
    bound and the deployment no limit. #}
{%- macro holds_on_heap(runtime, profile, tag, field) %}
impl {{ runtime }}::Holds{{ field.kind }}<{{ tag }}> for {{ profile }} {
{% if field.kind == "List" %}
{% if field.capacity is not none %}
    type List<T> = {{ runtime }}::CappedVec<T, {{ field.capacity }}> where T: Default + ::core::fmt::Debug + Clone + PartialEq;
{% else %}
    type List<T> = {{ runtime }}::GrowVec<T> where T: Default + ::core::fmt::Debug + Clone + PartialEq;
{% endif %}
{% elif field.kind == "Str" %}
    type Str = {% if field.capacity is not none %}{{ runtime }}::CappedStr<{{ field.capacity }}>{% else %}{{ runtime }}::GrowStr{% endif %};
{% else %}
    type Bytes = {% if field.capacity is not none %}{{ runtime }}::CappedBytes<{{ field.capacity }}>{% else %}{{ runtime }}::GrowBytes{% endif %};
{% endif %}
}
{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro declare(struct_name, runtime, fields, gated, bound, lent_bound, from_bound) %}
{% for field in fields %}
/// The field `{{ field.id }}` of `{{ struct_name }}`, which a storage profile
/// answers for by this type.
#[allow(dead_code)]
pub struct {{ field.tag }};

{% if field.capacity is not none %}
{{ holds(runtime, runtime ~ "::Inline", field.tag, field) }}

{% else %}
// `Inline` does not answer for `{{ field.id }}`: the protocol states no bound of
// it, so it is held only by a profile whose container grows, or by a deployment
// that gives it a capacity (docs/adr/0077 §7).

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
