{#- What the origin projection of a codec's owned form asks of a storage profile
    (`--owned-origin`, docs/adr/0077 §7): what `{Codec}Storage` asks, an origin
    profile, and for each byte string and text a container the profile builds
    from the origin, here and in each codec it holds. The profile chooses the
    container tag by tag, so a tag it gave none is a compile error at the
    projection, never a silent copy. Declared only with the option, so the
    default output is unchanged; a child under a build feature is reached
    through a trait of its own, as in `declare`. #}
{%- macro declare_origin(struct_name, gated, origin_bound) %}
{% for child in gated %}
{{ child.cfg }}
#[allow(dead_code)]
pub trait {{ child.helper }}Origin: {{ child.origin_bound }} {}

{{ child.cfg }}
impl<S: {{ child.origin_bound }}> {{ child.helper }}Origin for S {}

{{ child.cfg_off }}
#[allow(dead_code)]
pub trait {{ child.helper }}Origin {}

{{ child.cfg_off }}
impl<S> {{ child.helper }}Origin for S {}

{% endfor %}
/// What the origin projection of `{{ struct_name }}` asks of a storage profile
/// beside {{ struct_name }}Storage: that it is an origin profile, and
/// that each byte string and text of `{{ struct_name }}` and of the codecs it
/// holds is built from the origin by the container the profile holds it in.
#[allow(dead_code)]
pub trait {{ struct_name }}Origin: {{ origin_bound }} {}

impl<S: {{ origin_bound }}> {{ struct_name }}Origin for S {}
{% endmacro %}
